  "source_model": {
    "id": 6678,
    "name": "CD4+ T cell Differentiation",
    "description": "The model includes 38 components and 96 biochemical interactions that regulate the differentiation process of major T cell subtypes, i.e., Th1, Th2, Th17 and iTreg cells. Individual components of the model represent lineage-specifying transcription factors (Tbet, GATA3, ROR\u03b3t, and Foxp3), STAT proteins, cytokines, their receptors, and other signaling molecules. The extracellular environment is represented in the model by eight cytokines and a (generic) TCR ligand known to play a role in T cell differentiation. PMID: 22871178",
    "tags": "T helper cell, differentiation",
